<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Farrukhan the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 712–728</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Farrukhan the Great was the ispahbad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a>, the mountainous Caspian province of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, and the most powerful ruler of the Dabuyid dynasty. In 717 he defeated the invading army of the Umayyad general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-ibn-al-muhallab">Yazid ibn al-Muhallab</a> in the forests of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a>, forcing a treaty in which he paid only a modest tribute. His victory preserved the Dabuyids' independence for another generation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/farrukhan-the-great.jpg" alt="Farrukhan the Great" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Farrukhan_the_Great_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
